      "confirmed_facts": [
        {
          "fact_id": "f1",
          "text": "Computer Science > Artificial Intelligence [Submitted on 13 Jul 2026] Title:Distribird: Literature-Informed Prior Distribution Design for Bayesian Model Calibration View PDF HTML (experimental) Abstract:Bayesian calibration of process-based models requires a prior distribution fo",
          "source_id": "source:primary",
          "captured_at": "2026-08-14T08:04:25.255215+08:00",
          "content_sha256": "78c1bf4aae97378e5c05b28a4c6463d8703c9d6b0c2022312948634eaec597e1",
          "excerpt": "Computer Science > Artificial Intelligence [Submitted on 13 Jul 2026] Title:Distribird: Literature-Informed Prior Distribution Design for Bayesian Model Calibration View PDF HTML (experimental) Abstract:Bayesian calibration of process-based models requires a prior distribution fo",
          "sentence_hash": "4b82a30e4c647e138421d3f67d7d1dc6335cd6fd6f3f9ad33605728e79787384",
          "anchors": [
            "for",
            "Jul 20"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact_id": "f2",
          "text": "Despite decades of methodological work, researchers almost always fall back on uniform priors.",
          "source_id": "source:primary",
          "captured_at": "2026-08-14T08:04:25.255228+08:00",
          "content_sha256": "78c1bf4aae97378e5c05b28a4c6463d8703c9d6b0c2022312948634eaec597e1",
          "excerpt": "Despite decades of methodological work, researchers almost always fall back on uniform priors.",
          "sentence_hash": "543d74b78634e006929738a128c2ecce655d4bad2fb2a2d6fd178b76515f6704",
          "anchors": [
            "for"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact_id": "f3",
          "text": "The main reason is that building informative priors from scientific literature is slow and needs both domain and statistical expertise.",
          "source_id": "source:primary",
          "captured_at": "2026-08-14T08:04:25.255244+08:00",
          "content_sha256": "78c1bf4aae97378e5c05b28a4c6463d8703c9d6b0c2022312948634eaec597e1",
          "excerpt": "The main reason is that building informative priors from scientific literature is slow and needs both domain and statistical expertise.",
          "sentence_hash": "7d2babae8c2c9a15da8bed3ec8cc3e170602608909b4d26d293ce931adb03bda",
          "anchors": [
            "for",
            "literature",
            "ai"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact_id": "f4",
          "text": "Given a parameter name, physical description, and domain context, Distribird deploys a multi-agent pipeline that searches the literature, extracts and weights reported values by domain relevance, and fits a probability distribution via AIC model selection.",
          "source_id": "source:primary",
          "captured_at": "2026-08-14T08:04:25.255270+08:00",
          "content_sha256": "78c1bf4aae97378e5c05b28a4c6463d8703c9d6b0c2022312948634eaec597e1",
          "excerpt": "Given a parameter name, physical description, and domain context, Distribird deploys a multi-agent pipeline that searches the literature, extracts and weights reported values by domain relevance, and fits a probability distribution via AIC model selection.",
          "sentence_hash": "7d8d61f13c3df2586a08c33b352d489ef8af9d26129ffe4657876ea390ae949d",
          "anchors": [
            "literature",
            "ai"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact_id": "f5",
          "text": "When no literature is available, the system falls back to sensible uninformative alternatives, and clearly reports both the evidence behind and the confidence level of every prior it produces.",
          "source_id": "source:primary",
          "captured_at": "2026-08-14T08:04:25.255290+08:00",
          "content_sha256": "78c1bf4aae97378e5c05b28a4c6463d8703c9d6b0c2022312948634eaec597e1",
          "excerpt": "When no literature is available, the system falls back to sensible uninformative alternatives, and clearly reports both the evidence behind and the confidence level of every prior it produces.",
          "sentence_hash": "ffef14c95b463d31cef48531fa6898100cab74aebf66269675f3cff879f877d0",
          "anchors": [
            "for",
            "literature",
            "ai",
            "every"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact_id": "f6",
          "text": "It is designed for the problems where the models have physically interpretable parameters, where domain knowledge exists in the published literature.",
          "source_id": "source:primary",
          "captured_at": "2026-08-14T08:04:25.255305+08:00",
